[{:db/id 17592186055121 :question/problem "A solution to the linear equation $y=3x-2$ is the ordered pair $(4,t).$ What is the value of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $(4,t)$ is a solution to the linear equation $y=3x-2,$ the equation must turn into a true statement if we substitute $4$ and $t$ for $x$ and $y.$ So, we replace $x$ with $4$ and $y$ with $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-2 \\\\ (t) & =3(4)-2 \\\\ t & =12-2 \\\\ t & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186052094 :answer-field/correct 17592186052095 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054693 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8850735f-3807-552e-a696-83fed33439b4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8850735f-3807-552e-a696-83fed33439b4" :question/id #uuid "8850735f-3807-552e-a696-83fed33439b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-44331" :question/problem "Which of the following ordered pairs is **NOT** a solution to $y=3x+4?$\n\nI. $(4,16)$\n\nII. $(0,4)$\n\nIII. $(3,12)$" :question/worked-solution "To check whether each point is a solution to the equation, we substitute it into the equation and see if it results in a true statement.\n\nFirst, we substitute $(4,16)$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (16) & =3(4)+4 \\\\ 16 & =12+4 \\\\ 16 & =16\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a true statement, so $(4,16)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\nNext, we substitute $(0,4)$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (4) & =3(0)+4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is again a true statement, so $(0,4)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nFinally, we substitute $(3,12)$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (12) & =3(3)+4 \\\\ 12 & =9+4 \\\\ 12 & =13\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a false statement, so $(3,12)$ is *not* a solution to the equation.\n\nSo, out of the three ordered pairs given, the only pair that is *not* a solution to the equation is III $(3,12).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b78c8c28-e7f5-5c67-a2f4-7acc6b4dc795"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b78c8c28-e7f5-5c67-a2f4-7acc6b4dc795" :answer-field/id #uuid "b78c8c28-e7f5-5c67-a2f4-7acc6b4dc795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03a6c279-2e8a-5668-8055-0c5048d986d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-55cd2295-7391-5333-b505-2bebeab49eda" "answer-c46fb7a0-b425-5c37-9b0c-bf407dbdefee" "answer-c8246af6-e321-5c32-9d54-0be845fb1a81" "answer-ee218eec-e653-595b-ae8d-c1cb3b786e4e" "answer-03a6c279-2e8a-5668-8055-0c5048d986d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55cd2295-7391-5333-b505-2bebeab49eda" :answer/id #uuid "55cd2295-7391-5333-b505-2bebeab49eda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c46fb7a0-b425-5c37-9b0c-bf407dbdefee" :answer/id #uuid "c46fb7a0-b425-5c37-9b0c-bf407dbdefee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8246af6-e321-5c32-9d54-0be845fb1a81" :answer/id #uuid "c8246af6-e321-5c32-9d54-0be845fb1a81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee218eec-e653-595b-ae8d-c1cb3b786e4e" :answer/id #uuid "ee218eec-e653-595b-ae8d-c1cb3b786e4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03a6c279-2e8a-5668-8055-0c5048d986d9" :answer/id #uuid "03a6c279-2e8a-5668-8055-0c5048d986d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055294 :question/problem "Which of the following ordered pairs is **NOT** a solution to $y=\\frac{x}{4}?$\n\nI. $(-8,-2)$\n\nII. $(4,1)$\n\nIII. $(-4,1)$" :question/worked-solution "To check whether each point is a solution to the equation, we substitute it into the equation and see if it results in a true statement.\n\nFirst, we substitute $(-8,-2)$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ (-2) & =\\frac{-8}{4} \\\\ -2 & =-2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a true statement, so $(-8,-2)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\nNext, we substitute $(4,1)$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ (1) & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is again a true statement, so $(4,1)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nFinally, we substitute $(-4,1)$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ (1) & =\\frac{-4}{4} \\\\ 1 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a false statement, so $(-4,1)$ is *not* a solution to the equation.\n\nSo, out of the three ordered pairs given, the only pair that is *not* a solution to the equation is III $(-4,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186053001 :answer-field/correct 17592186053002 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-79379d05-b0be-5c61-ad3e-3f16014d5845" :activity/id #uuid "79379d05-b0be-5c61-ad3e-3f16014d5845" :activity/title "Two-Variable Linear Equations and Their Solutions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048714 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-25153cc4-0bb1-58a9-948e-484f2cd7ded3" "step-a685fca1-6658-58eb-8ca3-e22cbf302dbc" "step-006679ea-b5f9-5feb-a9ce-c5555dad089f"] :activity/first-step "step-25153cc4-0bb1-58a9-948e-484f2cd7ded3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-25153cc4-0bb1-58a9-948e-484f2cd7ded3" :step/id #uuid "25153cc4-0bb1-58a9-948e-484f2cd7ded3" :step/content 17592186055121 :step/next "step-a685fca1-6658-58eb-8ca3-e22cbf302dbc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a685fca1-6658-58eb-8ca3-e22cbf302dbc" :step/id #uuid "a685fca1-6658-58eb-8ca3-e22cbf302dbc" :step/content "question-8850735f-3807-552e-a696-83fed33439b4" :step/next "step-006679ea-b5f9-5feb-a9ce-c5555dad089f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-006679ea-b5f9-5feb-a9ce-c5555dad089f" :step/id #uuid "006679ea-b5f9-5feb-a9ce-c5555dad089f" :step/content 17592186055294 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186082517 :answer-field/choices 17592186082520] [:db/retract 17592186082517 :answer-field/choices 17592186082521] [:db/retract 17592186082517 :answer-field/choices 17592186082522] {:db/id 17592186083297 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cc46d129-8e8d-5162-b79e-c5e71e23455d" "question-e0b65e0b-a178-5086-8e32-4f470fc52a62" "question-2d0b4470-1f54-563e-803b-2a99b67b2c8a" "question-63a331e7-b7cc-5047-a29a-affb9857bb9b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083298 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6244a3eb-e8b2-58a8-937d-97547605cb0b" "question-709ee5be-390b-54a4-bcb8-cf4ff120d569"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083299 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1b9ba30c-75b9-548b-bbd4-b9dfefeaa769" "question-1e796ec1-771b-53ae-89e2-bbd160268b1c" "question-ec84be9a-d1c8-5ef5-8c9c-eaa63d5e60df" "question-7859a933-e507-551f-80d6-253f1a99b7af"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083080 :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](images/e1/e1b79fe61429e51171e07ceda9eefc6dcf727e59e7f6eb820fe64a0fe3041553.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ![](images/3a/3a6333dccc007be0992f95974a58ce3d652e5ecafcaaa865a24ff8b42bcfc37a.svg) is given by\n![](images/68/68085f6e83d4aba3b05bd631d523432bb0e664ceac36b8c707102ead6e0f9460.svg)\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) and ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n![](images/f5/f5250f1f7f213970a934f87b2bf9a59417348deaa854492e6c40d6a3c9ab8dc3.svg)\n\nTherefore, the center is ![](images/51/51c3c69238e5ffe9c22e9a9a50dd89f69899db2c0895c5f39e2d80db74c6b3db.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc46d129-8e8d-5162-b79e-c5e71e23455d" :question/id #uuid "cc46d129-8e8d-5162-b79e-c5e71e23455d" :question/math-academy-id "q-328252" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-7)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{20}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-7)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{20}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=7$ and $k=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,7,-2\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8eab0dc8-1d80-5e76-b822-61ea9413a58e" "answer-field-3b91c9dc-6bf7-59df-b1dd-24b768b44395"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8eab0dc8-1d80-5e76-b822-61ea9413a58e" :answer-field/id #uuid "8eab0dc8-1d80-5e76-b822-61ea9413a58e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-59e71ef8-7c90-5b08-b103-35f44f8511b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59e71ef8-7c90-5b08-b103-35f44f8511b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59e71ef8-7c90-5b08-b103-35f44f8511b8" :answer/id #uuid "59e71ef8-7c90-5b08-b103-35f44f8511b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b91c9dc-6bf7-59df-b1dd-24b768b44395" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b91c9dc-6bf7-59df-b1dd-24b768b44395" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5a56f004-5497-5387-89fd-6cffc2c9e0a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a56f004-5497-5387-89fd-6cffc2c9e0a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a56f004-5497-5387-89fd-6cffc2c9e0a6" :answer/id #uuid "5a56f004-5497-5387-89fd-6cffc2c9e0a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0b65e0b-a178-5086-8e32-4f470fc52a62" :question/id #uuid "e0b65e0b-a178-5086-8e32-4f470fc52a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-328265" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+9)^{2}}{25}-\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{100}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-9))^{2}}{25}-\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{100}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=-9$ and $k=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,-9,-3\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b13e1f0f-637e-5903-9e37-6c5b9b407ce4" "answer-field-51c45d36-de04-5e3d-9b97-b8d0d6373735"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b13e1f0f-637e-5903-9e37-6c5b9b407ce4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b13e1f0f-637e-5903-9e37-6c5b9b407ce4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d9379508-37f1-5d6c-a9c2-b7b30d359510" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9379508-37f1-5d6c-a9c2-b7b30d359510"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9379508-37f1-5d6c-a9c2-b7b30d359510" :answer/id #uuid "d9379508-37f1-5d6c-a9c2-b7b30d359510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51c45d36-de04-5e3d-9b97-b8d0d6373735" :answer-field/id #uuid "51c45d36-de04-5e3d-9b97-b8d0d6373735" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6b437ffd-5055-5a03-9b4b-06ba6ea646b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b437ffd-5055-5a03-9b4b-06ba6ea6