he graph from left to right, we can see that: \n\n- For $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)$ the graph rises\n\n- For $x\\in (-2,0)$ the graph falls\n\n- For $x\\in (0,2)$ the graph rises\n\n- For $x\\in (2,\\infty )$ the graph falls\n\nThe function is decreasing on the intervals where it never rises: $(-2,0)$ and $(2,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f88a252d-c8b0-5a96-ae23-b933c61e17fc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f88a252d-c8b0-5a96-ae23-b933c61e17fc" :answer-field/id #uuid "f88a252d-c8b0-5a96-ae23-b933c61e17fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1503f3b6-6628-565e-8d30-346cef745022" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98af19b4-c997-5827-8293-f65e22be1fe9" "answer-6e5663fa-292f-5ed0-8510-11cf8822cf69" "answer-6b8e57cd-e0b2-5f76-98c2-568e016f4008" "answer-1503f3b6-6628-565e-8d30-346cef745022" "answer-2b6c3128-d182-5d63-a456-93892359384d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98af19b4-c997-5827-8293-f65e22be1fe9" :answer/id #uuid "98af19b4-c997-5827-8293-f65e22be1fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e5663fa-292f-5ed0-8510-11cf8822cf69" :answer/id #uuid "6e5663fa-292f-5ed0-8510-11cf8822cf69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b8e57cd-e0b2-5f76-98c2-568e016f4008" :answer/id #uuid "6b8e57cd-e0b2-5f76-98c2-568e016f4008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1503f3b6-6628-565e-8d30-346cef745022" :answer/id #uuid "1503f3b6-6628-565e-8d30-346cef745022" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ and $(2,\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b6c3128-d182-5d63-a456-93892359384d" :answer/id #uuid "2b6c3128-d182-5d63-a456-93892359384d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\infty ,-2)$ and $(0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116429 :tutorial/content "A function ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) is **strictly increasing** if its ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value always rises as we increase the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value. No section of the graph is allowed to be flat.\n\n![](images/f6/f6136545f441473a1c873f7d3296e8d96c23357825ac442ce83ce313f2d74199.png)\n\nOn the other hand, a function ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) is **increasing** if its ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value *never falls* as we increase the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value. \n\n**Watch Out!** Increasing functions, like the one below, are allowed to have flat sections.\n\n![](images/b9/b979741f27906322c7ff290ae37bb5214c0c88d30e504fe18569c1f957e3d72e.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115437 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-18d3d63c-6302-5918-86bd-56e3b125a276" :activity/id #uuid "18d3d63c-6302-5918-86bd-56e3b125a276" :activity/title "Global vs. Local Extrema and Critical Points of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049676 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-5ced1b4f-bfff-54bd-81e3-f29078d59fc2" "step-1354966a-bc66-58aa-a442-7d67b1cd669b" "step-6cc3e502-2347-555d-b89f-52aa549d49ce" "step-3895ce48-ecf8-5610-add7-df9917d32e51" "step-5c591abe-52fa-53e7-961d-0fc811191f5e"] :activity/first-step "step-5ced1b4f-bfff-54bd-81e3-f29078d59fc2" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5ced1b4f-bfff-54bd-81e3-f29078d59fc2" :step/id #uuid "5ced1b4f-bfff-54bd-81e3-f29078d59fc2" :step/content 17592186124811 :step/next "step-1354966a-bc66-58aa-a442-7d67b1cd669b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1354966a-bc66-58aa-a442-7d67b1cd669b" :step/id #uuid "1354966a-bc66-58aa-a442-7d67b1cd669b" :step/content 17592186401426 :step/next "step-6cc3e502-2347-555d-b89f-52aa549d49ce" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6cc3e502-2347-555d-b89f-52aa549d49ce" :step/id #uuid "6cc3e502-2347-555d-b89f-52aa549d49ce" :step/content 17592186284447 :step/next "step-3895ce48-ecf8-5610-add7-df9917d32e51" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3895ce48-ecf8-5610-add7-df9917d32e51" :step/id #uuid "3895ce48-ecf8-5610-add7-df9917d32e51" :step/content 17592186434756 :step/next "step-5c591abe-52fa-53e7-961d-0fc811191f5e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5c591abe-52fa-53e7-961d-0fc811191f5e" :step/id #uuid "5c591abe-52fa-53e7-961d-0fc811191f5e" :step/content 17592186434761 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064355 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1c8e8af8-f023-59d2-a762-8f1491820c16"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064760 :question/problem "$-2+4.5=$" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-2+4.5=4.5-2=2.5\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062617 :answer-field/correct 17592186062622 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064356 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-89efd351-a602-5741-a803-e137883a9ffc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-89efd351-a602-5741-a803-e137883a9ffc" :question/id #uuid "89efd351-a602-5741-a803-e137883a9ffc" :question/math-academy-id "q-42784" :question/problem "$-1+\\frac{8}{5}=$" :question/worked-solution "We put both fractions over a common denominator of $5$ and then add the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-1+\\frac{8}{5}=-\\frac{5}{5}+\\frac{8}{5}=\\frac{-5+8}{5}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $8$ to $-5,$ we start at $-5$ on a number line and move $8$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/0b/0b6274b1cb65e330c81602212fe081835eb86c1c1c8e3a6eee278fbfd2614776.png)\n\nSo, $-5+8=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-5+8}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-5+8}{5}=\\frac{8-5}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-1+\\frac{8}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-246cfafb-6189-5729-9be6-ca9bbaab24e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-246cfafb-6189-5729-9be6-ca9bbaab24e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "246cfafb-6189-5729-9be6-ca9bbaab24e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a465af2b-dec0-551b-ba69-d768948fa6a0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0c6f050c-347c-5715-bfbc-fa64bfc3a91e" "answer-b200d3b9-1e60-511b-aaa3-c5cd7e7271c7" "answer-a465af2b-dec0-551b-ba69-d768948fa6a0" "answer-cf755884-e084-5588-aa54-d216bf7e6e7a" "answer-db32d174-5601-574a-a970-b10c4b349d19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c6f050c-347c-5715-bfbc-fa64bfc3a91e" :answer/id #uuid "0c6f050c-347c-5715-bfbc-fa64bfc3a91e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b200d3b9-1e60-511b-aaa3-c5cd7e7271c7" :answer/id #uuid "b200d3b9-1e60-511b-aaa3-c5cd7e7271c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a465af2b-dec0-551b-ba69-d768948fa6a0" :answer/id #uuid "a465af2b-dec0-551b-ba69-d768948fa6a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf755884-e084-5588-aa54-d216bf7e6e7a" :answer/id #uuid "cf755884-e084-5588-aa54-d216bf7e6e7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db32d174-5601-574a-a970-b10c4b349d19" :answer/id #uuid "db32d174-5601-574a-a970-b10c4b349d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c8e8af8-f023-59d2-a762-8f1491820c16" :question/id #uuid "1c8e8af8-f023-59d2-a762-8f1491820c16" :question/math-academy-id "q-128260" :question/problem "$-4.69+2.6=$" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-4.69+2.6=2.6-4.69=-2.09\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59340a3d-da2b-598b-9af5-fbf05febf9c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59340a3d-da2b-598b-9af5-fbf05febf9c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "59340a3d-da2b-598b-9af5-fbf05febf9c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b816418a-a268-5949-8a85-901c9d55dd6a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ecb71be-9558-5f7e-9c24-85c0d2bdee86" "answer-e209064d-2e8c-507a-bfa5-d4017ece1766" "answer-b816418a-a268-5949-8a85-901c9d55dd6a" "answer-0a1c250d-164f-5f47-9a26-9438d7f566ff" "answer-c029931b-c7eb-5a6d-a179-f9ea69c5f61e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ecb71be-9558-5f7e-9c24-85c0d2bdee86" :answer/id #uuid "8ecb71be-9558-5f7e-9c24-85c0d2bdee86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e209064d-2e8c-507a-bfa5-d4017ece1766" :answer/id #uuid "e209064d-2e8c-507a-bfa5-d4017ece1766" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b816418a-a268-5949-8a85-901c9d55dd6a" :answer/id #uuid "b816418a-a268-5949-8a85-901c9d55dd6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.09" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a1c250d-164f-5f47-9a26-9438d7f566ff" :answer/id #uuid "0a1c250d-164f-5f47-9a26-9438d7f566ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c029931b-c7eb-5a6d-a179-f9ea69c5f61e" :answer/id #uuid "c029931b-c7eb-5a6d-a179-f9ea69c5f61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c18cf1f6-b782-529c-9687-b480366e0abb" :activity/id #uuid "c18cf1f6-b782-529c-9687-b480366e0abb" :activity/title "Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048546 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-85d85619-b8de-50f5-92ee-a08b512ce531" "step-0efb6d7a-37b4-5a9c-baab-888a01b1d387" "step-e6925eb7-f263-5012-a586-f8fa6ea699aa"] :activity/first-step "step-85d85619-b8de-50f5-92ee-a08b512ce531" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-85d85619-b8de-50f5-92ee-a08b512ce531" :step/id #uuid "85d85619-b8de-50f5-92ee-a08b512ce531" :step/content 17592186064760 :step/next "step-0efb6d7a-37b4-5a9c-baab-888a01b1d387" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0efb6d7a-37b4-5a9c-baab-888a01b1d387" :step/id #uuid "0efb6d7a-37b4-5a9c-baab-888a01b1d387" :step/content "question-89efd351-a602-5741-a803-e137883a9ffc" :step/next "step-e6925eb7-f263-5012-a586-f8fa6ea699aa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e6925eb7-f263-5012-a586-f8fa6ea699aa" :step/id #uuid "e6925eb7-f263-5012-a586-f8fa6ea699aa" :step/content "question-1c8e8af8-f023-59d2-a762-8f1491820c16" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-14d93e8f-2ff1-562e-a35c-f8de5c3818d2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-14d93e8f-2ff1-562e-a35c-f8de5c3818d2" :question/id #uuid "14d93e8f-2ff1-562e-a35c-f8de5c3818d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-40857" :question/problem "$(-5.5)^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to calculate the product of $-5.5$ with itself:\n\n$$\n(-5.5)^{2}=(-5.5)\\cdot (-5.5)=(5.5)\\cdot (5.5)\n$$\n\nFirst, we ignore the decimal points and multiply as if both numbers were whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{2} \\\\ \\boxed{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $55\\times 55=3\\,025.$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in the first factor ($5.5$) and $1$ decimal place in the second factor ($5.5$), so their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nWe take our value of $3\\,025$ and insert a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places:\n\n$$\n30\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{25}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${5.5}^{2}=30.25.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c64d54dd-1bd9-5b4c-bf85-d147344d6818"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c64d54dd-1bd9-5b4c-bf85-d147344d6818" :answer-field/id #uuid "c64d54dd-1bd9-5b4c-bf85-d147344d6818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68e4b1c8-a132-5e30-a98b-556a99af5dac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4c01550-6c48-50cb-af06-6cd887f27626" "answer-552d15ae-c5c8-509e-8ca8-494431dec439" "answer-68e4b1c8-a132-5e30-a98b-556a99af5dac" "answer-ffd4bfdb-d6a7-556d-9522-25b678ff5a2c" "answer-996044d0-4829-58b0-acf3-4fda7d419060"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4c01550-6c48-50cb-